n he  was only 18.  we already know a few things about the  10th hunger games thanks to some  references made in the original trilogy  all of this information already appears  in the books but we'll warn you there  are a few spoilers ahead if you want to  go into the prequel blind  first we know that district 2 tribute  griffin naismith ends up winning the  10th edition of the games  we can expect to see him be even worse  than some of the most memorable violent  tributes like cato and clove  but of course griffin winning means that  snow's district 12 tribute doesn't  will losing his tribute affects knows  mental health will this be what sent him  down a cruel path towards the presidency  this brings us to another piece of  knowledge about the 10th games  there is a very good chance they were  rigged it's no secret that the capital  has picked favorites over the years  there should be 74 victors in total but  there's actually 88  officially listed this means that some  of the games were definitely  tampered with or the records of those  games were rewritten and that's why  collins is choosing to focus on  this tournament it could be the start of  snow's bitterness his tribute could have  been the one closest to winning the  games before the game maker picked a  favorite  and ruined everything and speaking of  game makers we know that seneca crane  the maker of the 74th games  is definitely not in this one instead  the 10th hunger games was controlled by  lucas castor the second ever game maker  who started his career during the 6th  annual hunger games  by the time we get to see him in the  prequel he'll have already had four  years of preparing  fatal arena challenges under his belt  caster's plans for the 10th hunger games  are going to be a nightmare for the  tributes  but maybe we'll get to see how seneca  was inspired by the historic game maker  that's it that's excellent  so why did suzanne collins decide to  pick the villain as the focus of her new  novel  w